      "content": "You are right to be on guard for escalation, as true outright hostility often hides under the guise of \"giving you space\" or \"realigning expectations.\" Look for signs like sudden shifts in your job description without discussion, isolation tactics where you are denied access to shared spaces or projects, or informal messages from multiple leaders attempting to pressure you to leave. If you notice managers beginning to ignore your requests or other employees refusing to acknowledge you, those are critical indicators of a coordinated exit strategy rather than just bad luck. Documenting these new behaviors immediately is crucial because they serve as direct evidence that the company is actively trying to terminate your employment legally or illegally.",
